{"parentUuid":"3f604316-2f41-4927-9119-b331c4901c2b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e58773f4-795c-461a-8921-8285de9967c6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0162Pbsg7QHRvwHsWQ3HEFYr","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Prime-Silo Home Directory Configuration\n2\t\n3\t## Overview\n4\t\n5\tThe **Home Directory** is where Prime-Silo stores its workspace data, including configuration, logs, and customware modules (L1, L2). On the desktop EXE, this location is now discoverable and configurable via the system tray.\n6\t\n7\t## Finding Your Home Directory\n8\t\n9\t### On Windows/Linux\n10\t\n11\t1. **Right-click the Prime-Silo system tray icon** (bottom right of taskbar)\n12\t2. Look for the line: **`Home: <directory name>`**\n13\t3. Click it to open the folder in your file explorer\n14\t\n15\t### On macOS\n16\t\n17\t1. **Right-click the Prime-Silo menu bar icon** (top right)\n18\t2. Look for the line: **`Home: <directory name>`**\n19\t3. Click it to open the folder in Finder\n20\t\n21\tIf the home directory is not configured, it will show: **`Home: (not configured)`**\n22\t\n23\t## Configuring the Home Directory\n24\t\n25\t### First-Time Setup\n26\t\n27\t1. Right-click the Prime-Silo system tray icon\n28\t2. Click **\"Configure Home Directory...\"**\n29\t3. Select (or create) a folder where you want to store Prime-Silo workspace data\n30\t4. Click **\"Select Folder\"** to confirm\n31\t\n32\tThe path will be saved and persists across restarts.\n33\t\n34\t### Changing the Home Directory\n35\t\n36\tTo change the home directory later:\n37\t\n38\t1. Right-click the system tray icon\n39\t2. Click **\"Configure Home Directory...\"**\n40\t3. Select a different folder\n41\t4. **Note:** You may need to restart Prime-Silo for some changes to take effect\n42\t\n43\t## For Agents & Scripts\n44\t\n45\tAgents and scripts running inside Prime-Silo can now query the configured home directory:\n46\t\n47\t```javascript\n48\t// In Electron preload or IPC context\n49\tconst { homeDir } = await ipcRenderer.invoke(\"space-desktop:get-home-directory\");\n50\tconsole.log(\"Configured home:\", homeDir);\n51\t// Returns: { homeDir: \"/path/to/home\" } or { homeDir: null }\n52\t```\n53\t\n54\tThis makes it possible for agents to:\n55\t\n56\t- Know where the workspace is located\n57\t- Access workspace-relative paths\n58\t- Configure their own workspace initialization\n59\t\n60\t## Troubleshooting\n61\t\n62\t### \"Home: (not configured)\"\n63\t\n64\tIf you see this message, no home directory has been set yet. Click **\"Configure Home Directory...\"** to set one up.\n65\t\n66\t### Home directory won't open\n67\t\n68\tMake sure the directory still exists. If you've moved or deleted the folder, use **\"Configure Home Directory...\"** to point to the correct location.\n69\t\n70\t### Changes not taking effect\n71\t\n72\tSome changes require a restart of Prime-Silo. Close the app completely (use tray \"Quit\") and reopen it.\n73\t\n74\t## Default Behavior\n75\t\n76\tIf no home directory is configured:\n77\t\n78\t- The app uses its default internal workspace (if one exists)\n79\t- To make this explicit, configure one using the tray menu\n80\t\n81\t## File Location\n82\t\n83\tThe home directory configuration is stored in:\n84\t\n85\t- **Windows:** `%APPDATA%\\Prime-Silo\\prime-silo-config.json`\n86\t- **macOS:** `~/Library/Application Support/Prime-Silo/prime-silo-config.json`\n87\t- **Linux:** `~/.config/Prime-Silo/prime-silo-config.json`\n88\t\n89\tYou can manually edit this JSON file if needed (format: `{ \"homeDir\": \"/path/to/home\" }`).\n90\t"}]},"uuid":"01b20fa6-6491-43d9-8e2d-4a6b62c51b73","timestamp":"2026-07-01T19:39:58.224Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo\\HOME-DIRECTORY.md","content":"# Prime-Silo Home Directory Configuration\n\n## Overview\n\nThe **Home Directory** is where Prime-Silo stores its workspace data, including configuration, logs, and customware modules (L1, L2). On the desktop EXE, this location is now discoverable and configurable via the system tray.\n\n## Finding Your Home Directory\n\n### On Windows/Linux\n\n1. **Right-click the Prime-Silo system tray icon** (bottom right of taskbar)\n2. Look for the line: **`Home: <directory name>`**\n3. Click it to open the folder in your file explorer\n\n### On macOS\n\n1. **Right-click the Prime-Silo menu bar icon** (top right)\n2. Look for the line: **`Home: <directory name>`**\n3. Click it to open the folder in Finder\n\nIf the home directory is not configured, it will show: **`Home: (not configured)`**\n\n## Configuring the Home Directory\n\n### First-Time Setup\n\n1. Right-click the Prime-Silo system tray icon\n2. Click **\"Configure Home Directory...\"**\n3. Select (or create) a folder where you want to store Prime-Silo workspace data\n4. Click **\"Select Folder\"** to confirm\n\nThe path will be saved and persists across restarts.\n\n### Changing the Home Directory\n\nTo change the home directory later:\n\n1. Right-click the system tray icon\n2. Click **\"Configure Home Directory...\"**\n3. Select a different folder\n4. **Note:** You may need to restart Prime-Silo for some changes to take effect\n\n## For Agents & Scripts\n\nAgents and scripts running inside Prime-Silo can now query the configured home directory:\n\n```javascript\n// In Electron preload or IPC context\nconst { homeDir } = await ipcRenderer.invoke(\"space-desktop:get-home-directory\");\nconsole.log(\"Configured home:\", homeDir);\n// Returns: { homeDir: \"/path/to/home\" } or { homeDir: null }\n```\n\nThis makes it possible for agents to:\n\n- Know where the workspace is located\n- Access workspace-relative paths\n- Configure their own workspace initialization\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### \"Home: (not configured)\"\n\nIf you see this message, no home directory has been set yet. Click **\"Configure Home Directory...\"** to set one up.\n\n### Home directory won't open\n\nMake sure the directory still exists. If you've moved or deleted the folder, use **\"Configure Home Directory...\"** to point to the correct location.\n\n### Changes not taking effect\n\nSome changes require a restart of Prime-Silo. Close the app completely (use tray \"Quit\") and reopen it.\n\n## Default Behavior\n\nIf no home directory is configured:\n\n- The app uses its default internal workspace (if one exists)\n- To make this explicit, configure one using the tray menu\n\n## File Location\n\nThe home directory configuration is stored in:\n\n- **Windows:** `%APPDATA%\\Prime-Silo\\prime-silo-config.json`\n- **macOS:** `~/Library/Application Support/Prime-Silo/prime-silo-config.json`\n- **Linux:** `~/.config/Prime-Silo/prime-silo-config.json`\n\nYou can manually edit this JSON file if needed (format: `{ \"homeDir\": \"/path/to/home\" }`).\n","numLines":90,"startLine":1,"totalLines":90}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3f604316-2f41-4927-9119-b331c4901c2b","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16","sessionId":"82feebf3-e8fe-4530-929e-4550be5527b2","version":"2.1.197","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
