{"parentUuid":"13818418-a1cd-4371-a814-3894a9e38285","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_01Ls1QbkF7L7FyrrLH4V6rYN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The plan is written to [PLAN-home-unification-and-ui-status.md](prime-silo/architecture/PLAN-home-unification-and-ui-status.md). Here's the TLDR:\n\n**Why it feels disconnected — I found four competing \"homes\" that only agree by accident:**\n\n1. Tray \"Configure Home Directory…\" writes `config.homeDir` — but almost nothing reads it besides the IPC query.\n2. Tray \"Configure **Benny** Home…\" writes a *separate* key `config.bennyHome`, and that's what actually drives the runtime supervisor's `BENNY_HOME` ([runtime_supervisor.js:56](prime-silo/packaging/desktop/runtime_supervisor.js:56)).\n3. `CUSTOMWARE_PATH` (the Space server's data root) follows neither — packaged builds hardcode it to `userData/customware` ([main.js:825](prime-silo/packaging/desktop/main.js:825)), dev mode takes it from env/args.\n4. When `BENNY_HOME` is unset, [workspace.py:18](prime-silo/runtime/benny/core/workspace.py:18) silently falls back to a repo-relative `workspace/` dir, and `benny init` writes wrapper scripts into the repo root — which is exactly why your git checkout now contains a populated `home/` tree, a `workspace/` dir, and `runtime/` full of `run_output*.txt` / `fix_ports*.py` debris.\n\n**On UI status:** the backend already has everything — SSE streams in `live_routes.py` and friends, plus per-run lineage endpoints and the `lineage_timeline`/`drilldown_table`/`reasoning_trace` widgets. But no screen consumes the SSE; every screen rolls its own `setInterval` poller (mission_control, lifelog, bridge's deep-produce and studio-cell pollers), and there's no global \"what's running\" surface, so a run started in one screen is invisible everywhere else.\n\n**The plan, in four phases:**\n\n- **Phase 0 (½ day):** repo hygiene — purge the `runtime/` scratch debris, archive the in-repo `home/`/`workspace/` state, gitignore regressions, stop `benny init` writing into the repo.\n- **Phase 1 (2–3 days):** one `PRIME_SILO_HOME` with `customware/` and `benny/` derived under it; a single resolver shared by Electron, the Node CLI, and Python (env > tray config > per-user default); one tray entry instead of two; the repo-relative fallback becomes a loud failure; `/api/home` + `benny doctor` report the resolved paths *with provenance*; legacy configs honored with an opt-in migration — never auto-moving data.\n- **Phase 2 (3–4 days):** a fan-in `/live/events` SSE on the runtime, one shared `activity-store.js` in the frontend (SSE with poll fallback) replacing all the per-screen timers, a persistent activity indicator with per-stage progress from lineage and click-through into the existing lineage widgets, plus one canonical status enum/color mapping in colors.css.\n- **Phase 3 (1–2 days):** rewrite HOME-DIRECTORY.md as the single home reference, add a first-run \"Home\" step to Setup, and a \"Where is my data?\" panel driven by `/api/home`.\n\nThe main risk is migrating existing installs that have `config.bennyHome` pointing at a lived-in home — the plan handles that by honoring legacy keys indefinitely and only migrating on explicit user action. Say the word and I'll start on Phase 0."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":443,"cache_read_input_tokens":91036,"output_tokens":1212,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":443,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1212,"cache_read_input_tokens":91036,"cache_creation_input_tokens":443,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":443},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ccbu