{"parentUuid":"c8d1c653-c73f-4c97-8d7b-e4e9ea955632","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo\\CLAUDE.md","snippet":"1\t# Prime-Silo Agent Navigation\n2\t\n3\t> For Claude and other agents working on Prime-Silo\n4\t\n5\t---\n6\t\n7\t## Current Status (as of 2026-06-17)\n8\t\n9\t**Latest Release:** v1.2.4 (PUBLISHED)  \n10\t**Documentation:** Complete overhaul with QUICKSTART-EXE.md, CLI.md, AGENT-AWARENESS.md, INDEX.md  \n11\t**All Packages:** Built and published for 6 platforms (Windows, macOS, Linux × x64 + ARM64)\n12\t\n13\t---\n14\t\n15\t## Architecture in One Sentence\n16\t\n17\tPrime-Silo is a deterministic execution platform (Benny runtime backend + Space-Agent React frontend) with two zones: deterministic manifests (read-only for agents) and a review sandbox (where agents can draft views and analyses). All changes are signed, versioned, and auditable.\n18\t\n19\t---\n20\t\n21\t## What Agents Need to Know\n22\t\n23\t### 1. Agent Authority (Strict Boundaries)\n24\t\n25\t**You CAN:**\n26\t\n27\t- ✅ Read manifests from L1/ and L2/\n28\t- ✅ Read past runs and lineage\n29\t- ✅ Query system state (home directory, config, graphs)\n30\t- ✅ Create draft views in `agent_sandbox/views/`\n31\t- ✅ Write analyses to `agent_sandbox/drafts/`\n32\t- ✅ Query memory graph and sessions\n33\t- ✅ Generate AI-powered reports and analyses\n34\t- ✅ Plan manifests (advisory, not executed)\n35\t\n36\t**You CANNOT:**\n37\t\n38\t- ❌ Execute manifests directly (`benny run` / `benny pypes run`)\n39\t- ❌ Mutate files in L1/ or L2/ (requires human signature)\n40\t- ❌ Delete or modify run history\n41\t- ❌ Sign or pin views (only humans can)\n42\t- ❌ Change configuration files\n43\t- ❌ Write outside `agent_sandbox/`\n44\t\n45\t**Why:** ADR-001 determinism boundary. Deterministic zone is read-only for agents; review zone (agent_sandbox) is where you draft and humans approve.\n46\t\n47\tSee **[AGENT-AWARENESS.md](AGENT-AWARENESS.md)** for complete details.\n48\t\n49\t### 2. System State Queries\n50\t\n51\t**Home Directory (Electron desktop):**\n52\t\n53\t```javascript\n54\t// Full resolved report: { homeDir, home: { root, source, bennyHome, customwarePath, warnings } }\n55\tconst { home } = await ipcRenderer.invoke(\"space-desktop:get-home-directory\");\n56\t// Or, from anywhere with server access: fetch(\"/api/home\") — same report + provenance.\n57\t// Returns: \"/path/to/workspace\" or null\n58\t```\n59\t\n60\t**Configuration:**\n61\t\n62\t```bash\n63\tfetch(\"/api/config\").then(r => r.json())  // All runtime config\n64\t```\n65\t\n66\t**Registered Manifests:**\n67\t\n68\t```bash\n69\tnode space registry           # List all manifests\n70\tfetch(\"/api/manifests\")       # Via API\n71\t```\n72\t\n73\t**Run History:**\n74\t\n75\t```bash\n76\tbenny runs ls --limit 10      # Past 10 runs\n77\tfetch(\"/api/runs?limit=10\")   # Via API\n78\t```\n79\t\n80\t**Memory Graph:**\n81\t\n82\t```bash\n83\tnode space memory status      # Check if Memo-Ray connected\n84\tnode space memory search \"<query>\"  # Search sessions\n85\t```\n86\t\n87\t### 3. APIs You Can Use\n88\t\n89\tSee **[AGENT-AWARENESS.md](AGENT-AWARENESS.md)** for complete API reference.\n90\t\n91\t**Key endpoints:**\n92\t\n93\t- `/api/config` — Runtime configuration\n94\t- `/api/manifests` — Registered manifests\n95\t- `/api/runs` — Run history\n96\t- `/api/graph/*` — Knowledge/code graphs\n97\t- `/api/lifelog` — Session activity feed\n98\t- `/api/integration_audit` — Check service status\n99\t\n100\t### 4. Skills Available\n101\t\n102\t**benny-pilot** — Manifest and run introspection\n103\t\n104\t```javascript\n105\tconst pilot = await import(\"/mod/_prime_silo/memoray_client/ext/skills/benny-pilot/benny-pilot.js\");\n106\t// Methods: queryManifests(), inspectRun(), etc.\n107\t```\n108\t\n109\t**memory-recall** — Session history\n110\t\n111\t```javascript\n112\tconst recall =\n113\t  await import(\"/mod/_prime_silo/memoray_client/ext/skills/memory-recall/memory-recall.js\");\n114\t// Methods: search(), getSessionContext(), etc.\n115\t```\n116\t\n117\t**project-guide** — Project-specific knowledge\n118\t\n119\t```javascript\n120\t// Available when working in the app\n121\t// Provides project context and suggestions\n122\t```\n123\t\n124\t---\n125\t\n126\t## How to Get Help\n127\t\n128\t### Finding What You Need\n129\t\n130\t| Question                             | Go to                                           |\n131\t| ------------------------------------ | ----------------------------------------------- |\n132\t| \"How do I set up the desktop app?\"   | [QUICKSTART-EXE.md](QUICKSTART-EXE.md)          |\n133\t| \"What CLI commands are available?\"   | [CLI.md](CLI.md)                                |\n134\t| \"What can I do as an agent?\"         | [AGENT-AWARENESS.md](AGENT-AWARENESS.md)        |\n135\t| \"Where is everything documented?\"    | [INDEX.md](INDEX.md)                            |\n136\t| \"How does the release process work?\" | [DEVOPS.md](DEVOPS.md)                          |\n137\t| \"What's the project architecture?\"   | [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) + [README.md](README.md) |\n138\t| \"How do I use the CLI?\"              | [GUIDE.md](GUIDE.md)                            |\n139\t\n140\t### Common Tasks\n141\t\n142\t**Check current version:**\n143\t\n144\t```bash\n145\tnode space version\n146\tcat package.json | jq .version\n147\t```\n148\t\n149\t**Explore workspace:**\n150\t\n151\t```bash\n152\t# Read config\n153\tfetch(\"/api/config\").then(r => r.json())\n154\t\n155\t# List manifests\n156\tnode space registry\n157\t\n158\t# Get home directory (Electron)\n159\tawait ipcRenderer.invoke(\"space-desktop:get-home-directory\")\n160\t```\n161\t\n162\t**Analyze a run:**\n163\t\n164\t```bash\n165\t# Get run details\n166\tbenny runs inspect <run_id>\n167\t\n168\t# Get lineage\n169\tbenny pypes drilldown <run_id> <stage>\n170\t\n171\t# Generate analysis report\n172\tbenny pypes agent-report <run_id>\n173\t```\n174\t\n175\t**Create a draft:**\n176\t\n177\t```javascript\n178\t// Write to sandbox\n179\tconst draft = {\n180\t  format: \"aamp.view/1\",\n181\t  title: \"My Analysis\",\n182\t  created_from_run: \"<run_id>\",\n183\t  panels: [...]\n184\t};\n185\t\n186\tfetch(\"/api/files/agent_sandbox/views/analysis.draft.view\", {\n187\t  method: \"POST\",\n188\t  body: JSON.stringify(draft)\n189\t});\n190\t```\n191\t\n192\t---\n193\t\n194\t## Release Process (For Handoff)\n195\t\n196\t**If you need to create a release, see [DEVOPS.md](DEVOPS.md).**\n197\t\n198\tQuick version:\n199\t\n200\t1. Make sure all changes are committed to main\n201\t2. Run: `node scripts/manage-release.js [patch|minor|major]`\n202\t3. Push commits: `git push origin main`\n203\t4. Push tag: `git push origin v1.2.X`\n204\t5. Wait ~30 minutes for all platforms to build\n205\t6. Release published to GitHub automatically\n206\t\n207\t**Critical:** Always push main before pushing tag, or build jobs will be skipped!\n208\t\n209\t---\n210\t\n211\t## Project Layout\n212\t\n213\t```\n214\tprime-silo/\n215\t├── README.md                    ← Start here\n216\t├── INDEX.md                     ← Doc navigation\n217\t├── QUICKSTART-EXE.md           ← Desktop app setup\n218\t├── CLI.md                       ← All commands\n219\t├── AGENT-AWARENESS.md          ← You are here (agent perms)\n220\t├── GUIDE.md                     ← UI walkthrough\n221\t├── DEVOPS.md                    ← Release process\n222\t├── HOME-DIRECTORY.md            ← Workspace structure\n223\t├── AGENTS.md                    ← Architecture contracts\n224\t├── CLAUDE.md                    ← This file\n225\t│\n226\t├── app/                         ← React frontend\n227\t├── server/                      ← Node.js API server\n228\t├── commands/                    ← CLI commands\n229\t├── packaging/                   ← Desktop build (Electron)\n230\t├── runtime/                     ← Vendored Benny backend\n231\t├── 