ared home, resolved once, derived everywhere\nd252406 gitignore: un-ignore runtime/tests/release (swallowed by the unanchored 'release' build-output rule)\n082b1ae Phase 0 repo hygiene: purge run debris, untrack scratch/worktree litter, stop init writing into the checkout","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"staleReadFileStateHint":"[This command modified 1 file you've previously read: HOME-DIRECTORY.md. Call Read before editing.]"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"35e8213e-492a-49d2-a0fb-b4185b1f0e80","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo","sessionId":"82feebf3-e8fe-4530-929e-4550be5527b2","version":"2.1.197","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"parentUuid":"0bcb00d7-844d-4180-8cbb-4d80ccd5cb62","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo\\HOME-DIRECTORY.md","snippet":"1\t# Prime-Silo Home — the single declared home\n2\t\n3\tPrime-Silo keeps all of its workspace data under **one declared home\n4\tdirectory**, with everything else derived from it:\n5\t\n6\t```\n7\t<home>/                       ← the declared Prime-Silo home\n8\t├── customware/               ← Space server data (L1/L2 modules)   → CUSTOMWARE_PATH\n9\t└── benny/                    ← portable Benny runtime              → $BENNY_HOME\n10\t    ├── bin/  config/  data/  workspaces/  models/  logs/  state/  …\n11\t```\n12\t\n13\tOne resolver decides where the home is, and every process — the desktop\n14\tshell, the tray, the Space server, `node space serve/supervise`, and the\n15\tPython runtime — asks the same resolver:\n16\t\n17\t- Node: `packaging/desktop/home_resolver.js` (`resolveHome()`)\n18\t- Python: `benny.portable.home.resolve_home()` / `resolve_benny_home()`\n19\t\n20\t## Resolution precedence (highest wins)\n21\t\n22\t| #   | Source                                                                 | Provenance tag |\n23\t| --- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------- |\n24\t| 1   | `PRIME_SILO_HOME` environment variable                                 | `env`          |\n25\t| 2   | `homeDir` in `prime-silo-config.json` (set via tray \"Configure Home…\") | `config`       |\n26\t| 3   | Per-user default: `<appData>/Prime-Silo/prime-silo-home`               | `default`      |\n27\t\n28\tDerived paths can still be overridden individually — an explicit\n29\t`BENNY_HOME` or `CUSTOMWARE_PATH` env var always wins for its own path —\n30\tbut the override is _reported_, not silent: it carries an `env-override`\n31\tsource tag and a divergence warning when it points outside the declared\n32\thome.\n33\t\n34\t**There is no repo-relative fallback.** Nothing writes into a git checkout\n35\twhen the home is unconfigured; the per-user default is used instead.\n36\t\n37\t## Checking where your home is (and why)\n38\t\n39\t- **Tray** — right-click the Prime-Silo tray icon: `Home: <name> (source)`\n40\t  with derived `Benny data:` and `Customware:` children. Click any of them\n41\t  to open the folder.\n42\t- **API** — `GET /api/home` on the Space server returns the resolved\n43\t  triple, each path's source, and any divergence warnings.\n44\t- **CLI** — `benny doctor` prints a `Home resolution` check with the same\n45\t  provenance; any legacy key or out-of-tree override shows as WARN.\n46\t- **Electron/IPC** — `ipcRenderer.invoke(\"space-desktop:get-home-directory\")`\n47\t  returns `{ homeDir, home }` where `home` is the full resolved report.\n48\t\n49\t## Configuring\n50\t\n51\t1. Right-click the tray icon → **\"Configure Home…\"** → pick (or create) a\n52\t   folder. `benny/` and `customware/` will live under it.\n53\t2. Restart Prime-Silo for the runtime to adopt the new location (the tray\n54\t   shows a `Runtime using: … (restart to apply new home)` line until then).\n55\t\n56\tThe setting persists in:\n57\t\n58\t- **Windows:** `%APPDATA%\\Prime-Silo\\prime-silo-config.json`\n59\t- **macOS:** `~/Library/Application Support/Prime-Silo/prime-silo-config.json`\n60\t- **Linux:** `~/.config/Prime-Silo/prime-silo-config.json`\n61\t\n62\tFormat: `{ \"homeDir\": \"/path/to/home\" }`.\n63\t\n64\t## Legacy installs\n65\t\n66\tOlder versions used three independent locations. All of them keep working —\n67\tnothing is moved automatically — but each is flagged so you can adopt the\n68\tunified layout when ready:\n69\t\n70\t| Legacy mechanism                                                            | Behavior now                                                                                                |\n71\t| --------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n72\t| `bennyHome` key in `prime-silo-config.json` (old \"Configure Benny Home…\")   | Honored (`legacy-config`); tray offers **\"Clear legacy Benny Home override\"** as the explicit adoption step |\n73\t| `<userData>/benny-home` and `<userData>/customware` (old per-user defaults) | Auto-detected when they exist (`legacy-default`) so existing data stays visible                             |\n74\t| `BENNY_HOME` env var pointing elsewhere                                     | Honored (`env-override`) with a divergence warning in doctor//api/home                                      |\n75\t\n76\tTo adopt the unified home: configure a home via the tray (or set\n77\t`PRIME_SILO_HOME`), move the contents of your old benny-home into\n78\t`<home>/benny/` and old customware into `<home>/customware/`, then clear\n79\tthe legacy override. `benny doctor` confirms when everything reports\n80\t`derived`.\n81\t\n82\t## For agents & scripts\n83\t\n84\t- Query `GET /api/home` instead of reading env vars.\n85\t- Python code must call `benny.portable.home.resolve_benny_home()` rather\n86\t  than `os.environ.get(\"BENNY_HOME\", <fallback>)` — cwd-relative fallbacks\n87\t  are how run debris used to end up committed to the repo.\n88\t- Node code (desktop/CLI/server) requires\n89\t  `packaging/desktop/home_resolver.js`.\n90\t\n91\t## Troubleshooting\n92\t\n93\t- **\"Runtime using: … (restart to apply new home)\"** in the tray — you\n94\t  reconfigured the home while the bundled runtime was running. Quit and\n95\t  reopen Prime-Silo.\n96\t- **Doctor WARNs about a legacy key or env override** — expected until you\n97\t  adopt the unified layout (see \"Legacy installs\"); the WARN is the\n98\t  tripwire, not an error.\n99\t- **Home folder won't open** — the directory no longer exists; reconfigure\n100\t  via the tray."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"acff2b33-19f0-4ead-a055-d0538d80202e",